296	     1	/**
297	     2	 * An item a policy covers, as the office records it.
298	     3	 *
299	     4	 * The office reads the recorded facts to classify the item's risk, so the
300	     5	 * classifications live here with the facts they read, while what each risk
301	     6	 * costs is the premium rules' business in {@link PremiumPolicy}. The
302	     7	 * enchantment level carries more than one such classification: the premium
