549	     8	 * The MHPCO price list: one published tariff row per insurable item type,
550	     9	 * stating what the office charges as that item's base premium and what it
551	    10	 * insures the item for. Main items are listed individually; every component
552	    11	 * shares one row, because the office prices and insures a rune exactly as it
553	    12	 * does a moonstone, and a building block of alike components is offered at a
554	    13	 * special rate.
555	    14	 *
556	    15	 * The block rate is the one tariff decision that is not a property of a single
557	    16	 * item: a block is a quantity of <em>alike</em> components, so the tariff also
558	    17	 * decides which items count as alike (see {@link #alikenessGroupOf}) and groups
559	    18	 * them before pricing.
560	    19	 *
561	    20	 * This is the office's tariff. It changes on its own schedule, independently of
562	    21	 * the modifier rules in {@link PremiumPolicy}.
563	    22	 */
564	    23	public class PriceList {
